o called a  general election when she said she  wouldn't and then refused to turn up at  all throughout this campaign she avoided  scrutiny like a vampire avoids the  sunlight we have a chancellor who went  AWOL for the whole campaign and why  because they have nothing to boast about  on the economy the subject which has  dared not speak its name in this  election I want to thank and  congratulate our leader Jeremy Corbyn he  campaigns he campaigned positively to  communicate the Labour values that we  share but let us not be complacent our  movement must continue to broaden its  reach and open its ears to ensure that  those who are not convinced by as this  time will be next time and I pledge to  play my part any part my party should  ask of me we face an incredibly  important task in the next few years  negotiating a new future that protects  jobs investment growth security and our  influence in a rapidly changing world  this election was called specifically on  brexit Theresa May said again and again  that this was about brexit well the  people have spoken they have rejected  Theresa Mays approach to brexit childish  pointless hostility to Europe combined  with an uncritical attitude to Donald  Trump  the real coalition of chaos Liam Fox  David Davis and Boris Johnson who spent  the election acting the fool and  brawling with my  and group win in these circumstances  Parliament must revisit the negotiating  strategy and play a central role in  managing the brexit negotiations with a  genuine parliamentary vote on any final  deal anything less would be unacceptable  so we've got a lot to get on with and I  would like to thank the people of  Wallasey for allowing me to represent  you in the next parliament I promise to  you to give my effort my dedication and  my complete commitment in the month  ahead thank you  [Applause]
 

